We thus have several essentially equivalent points of view, for describing by profinite means a finitely generated extension \inserted{$K$} of $\mathbb Q$ :

1) By the étale topos $B_K$, as a pro-Galois topos over $B_{\mathbb Q}$

2) By the fundamental groupoid $\Pi_K$ of this topos, (the groupoid of its points, or of its universal covers) --- as a groupoid over $\Pi_{\mathbb Q}$

\deleted{2)} 3) By the outer group $E_K$, over the outer group $E_{\mathbb Q}\longleftarrow\Gamma_{\mathbb Q}$ (pro-group)

4) In terms of an algebraic closure $\bar K/K$ (that is, by describing the pair $(K,\bar K)$ rather than $K$), by an object $\overline{\mathbb Q}\in\operatorname{Ob}\Pi_{\mathbb Q}$, and a homomorphism of profinite groups $\unsure{\mathcal E|E}\longrightarrow\Gamma_{\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q}$.
\deleted{an open subgroup $\Gamma$ of}

5) In terms of a \inserted{fixed} algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathbb Q$, \deleted{by the group}\inserted{and $\Gamma=\Gamma_{\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q}$}, \deleted{by} considering the pairs $(K,i)$ where $i:k\longrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is an embedding of the algebraic closure\inserted{$k$} of $\mathbb Q$ in $K$ into $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ : \deleted{\unsure{as}} by the outer group $\pi_K\neq\pi_1(K)$, on which an open subgroup $\Gamma_K\subset\Gamma$ acts by outer automorphisms.

\margin{6) In terms of a $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ : by the groupoid $\Pi_{K\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ (not necessarily connected) on which $\Gamma_{\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q}$ acts --- or else sometimes, by the Galois topos $B_{K\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\overline{\mathbb Q}}$, with $\Gamma_{\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q}$ acting on it\ldots}
